@startuml Prototype Pattern - Commission Calculator

' Define the styles
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classFontStyle bold
skinparam classBackgroundColor #f8f9fa
skinparam classBorderColor #dee2e6
skinparam arrowColor #6c757d
skinparam stereotypeCBackgroundColor #e9ecef

' Title
title Prototype Pattern - Deal Cloning Implementation

' Prototype Interface
interface Prototype<T> <<interface>> {
  +clone(): T
}

' Domain Models (Base Classes)
class Deal <<DomainModel>> {
  -id: String
  -title: String
  -value: BigDecimal
  -status: DealStatus
  -salesRepId: String
  -products: List<DealProduct>
  -closeDate: LocalDate
  -createdDate: LocalDate
  -lastModifiedDate: LocalDate
}

class DealProduct <<DomainModel>> {
  -id: String
  -productId: String
  -productName: String
  -quantity: int
  -price: BigDecimal
  -discount: BigDecimal
  -dealId: String
}

' Concrete Prototypes
class CloneableDeal <<ConcretePrototype>> {
  +CloneableDeal()
  +CloneableDeal(title: String, value: BigDecimal, salesRepId: String)
  +clone(): CloneableDeal
  +deepClone(): CloneableDeal
}

class CloneableDealProduct <<ConcretePrototype>> {
  +CloneableDealProduct()
  +CloneableDealProduct(productId: String, productName: String, quantity: int, price: BigDecimal)
  +clone(): CloneableDealProduct
}

' Prototype Registry
class PrototypeRegistry <<Registry>> {
  -prototypes: Map<String, CloneableDeal>
  +PrototypeRegistry()
  +addPrototype(key: String, prototype: CloneableDeal): void
  +getPrototype(key: String): CloneableDeal
  +removePrototype(key: String): void
  +containsPrototype(key: String): boolean
  +size(): int
  +clear(): void
  +getKeys(): Iterable<String>
}

' Enum
enum DealStatus <<Enum>> {
  OPEN
  WON
  LOST
  PENDING
}

' Relationships
Prototype <|.. CloneableDeal : implements
Prototype <|.. CloneableDealProduct : implements
Deal <|-- CloneableDeal : extends
DealProduct <|-- CloneableDealProduct : extends
CloneableDeal o--> "*" CloneableDealProduct : contains
CloneableDeal --> "1" DealStatus : has status
PrototypeRegistry o--> "*" CloneableDeal : stores
CloneableDeal ..> CloneableDeal : clones
CloneableDealProduct ..> CloneableDealProduct : clones

' Pattern component notes
note right of Prototype
  <b>Prototype Interface</b>
  Generic interface defining
  the clone contract.

  <b>Type Parameter T:</b>
  Allows each prototype to
  return its own type from clone().

  <b>Design Benefit:</b>
  Type-safe cloning without
  casting required.
end note

note top of CloneableDeal
  <b>Concrete Prototype: CloneableDeal</b>

  Extends Deal domain model and implements
  Prototype interface for cloning capabilities.

  <b>Two Cloning Strategies:</b>

  • <b>clone():</b> Shallow copy
    - Copies all primitive fields
    - Creates new ArrayList for products
    - But shares product references
    - Fast but modifications affect both

  • <b>deepClone():</b> Deep copy
    - Copies all primitive fields
    - Clones each product individually
    - Complete independence from original
    - Safer but more expensive

  <b>Use Cases:</b>
  • Template deals for sales reps
  • Historical deal recreation
  • Test data generation
  • Deal variations (same structure, different values)
end note

note bottom of CloneableDealProduct
  <b>Concrete Prototype: CloneableDealProduct</b>

  Cloneable version of DealProduct.

  <b>Clone Implementation:</b>
  • Creates new instance
  • Copies all 7 fields
  • Returns independent copy

  <b>Why Needed:</b>
  Required for deep cloning of Deal
  to ensure complete independence.
end note

note left of PrototypeRegistry
  <b>Prototype Registry</b>

  Centralized catalog of pre-configured
  deal templates.

  <b>Purpose:</b>
  • Store standard deal types
    (standard, premium, enterprise)
  • Quick retrieval by name
  • Avoid recreating templates

  <b>Workflow:</b>
  1. Create & configure prototype deals
  2. Register with meaningful keys
  3. Retrieve prototype by key
  4. Clone and customize for new deal

  <b>Benefits:</b>
  • Standardizes deal configurations
  • Reduces initialization code
  • Centralized template management
  • Runtime prototype modification
end note

note right of DealStatus
  <b>Enum</b>
  Deal lifecycle states.

  Immutable, safe to share
  between clones.
end note

' Usage examples
note bottom of CloneableDeal
  <b>Usage Example - Shallow Clone:</b>

  CloneableDeal prototype = new CloneableDeal(
      "Standard Deal", new BigDecimal("10000"), "REP-001");
  prototype.setStatus(DealStatus.OPEN);
  prototype.addProduct(product);

  // Clone creates new deal with same structure
  CloneableDeal newDeal = prototype.clone();
  newDeal.setId("DEAL-NEW-1");
  newDeal.setTitle("Custom Deal");
  // Products list is new, but references same product objects

  <b>Usage Example - Deep Clone:</b>

  // Deep clone for complete independence
  CloneableDeal fullyIndependent = prototype.deepClone();
  fullyIndependent.setId("DEAL-NEW-2");
  // Modifying products won't affect prototype
end note

note bottom of PrototypeRegistry
  <b>Registry Usage Example:</b>

  // Setup: Create and register templates
  PrototypeRegistry registry = new PrototypeRegistry();

  CloneableDeal standardTemplate = createStandardDeal();
  CloneableDeal premiumTemplate = createPremiumDeal();

  registry.addPrototype("standard", standardTemplate);
  registry.addPrototype("premium", premiumTemplate);

  // Usage: Retrieve and clone
  CloneableDeal newDeal = registry
      .getPrototype("premium")
      .deepClone();

  newDeal.setId("DEAL-001");
  newDeal.setSalesRepId("REP-002");
  // Now have independent premium deal with custom values
end note

' Problem/Solution note
note top of Deal
  <b>Domain Model (Base Class)</b>

  Original Deal class from domain model.
  Not directly cloneable.

  <b>Problem:</b>
  Deal creation can be complex:
  • Many fields to set
  • Products to add
  • Status and dates to configure

  <b>Solution:</b>
  Create pre-configured prototype deals
  and clone them to create new instances.

  <b>Benefits vs Builder:</b>
  • Builder: Build new from scratch
  • Prototype: Copy existing configuration
  • Both: Avoid complex initialization
  • Use together: Build prototype once,
    clone many times
end note

' Legend
note right of CloneableDealProduct
  <b>Prototype Pattern in Commission Calculator:</b>

  <b>Problem Solved:</b>
  Creating similar Deal objects requires:
  • Repeating same initialization code
  • Re-adding same products
  • Reconfiguring same settings
  • Error-prone manual copying

  <b>Prototype Solution:</b>
  • Create template deals once
  • Clone to create new instances
  • Customize only what changes
  • Shallow or deep copy as needed

  <b>Implementation Pattern:</b>
  1. CloneableDeal extends Deal
  2. Implements Prototype<CloneableDeal>
  3. Provides clone() and deepClone()
  4. Registry stores common templates

  <b>Shallow vs Deep Cloning:</b>
  • <b>Shallow:</b> Fast, shares product objects
    Use when products won't change
  • <b>Deep:</b> Complete copy, independent
    Use when products will be modified

  <b>Key Benefits:</b>
  • Avoid complex deal creation code
  • Reuse standard configurations
  • Create deal variations quickly
  • Registry provides template catalog
  • Works well with Builder pattern

  <b>Real-World Usage:</b>
  • Standard deal templates per region
  • Product bundle templates
  • Historical deal recreation
  • Test data generation
  • Deal proposal variations
end note

@enduml